From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:54:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 23/56] Colour fenced code blocks in the Markdown preview

Code blocks with a language tag (json, bash, sh, python, rust, ...) get
syntax colours in Preview and Split, from the editor's own syntax set and
syntax theme, so they look as in the Source view and follow the light /
dark switch. No tag, an unknown tag or a block over 2000 lines stays
plain. Highlighted blocks are cached by theme, language and code, so a
re-parse while typing in Split only highlights the blocks that changed;
blocks no longer shown are dropped on the next parse.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

